# =====================================================================
# Cumulative analysis script (step00-step13)
#   step00: download the ReSTLess Open Database (v2 main, v1 for comparison); skipped if files exist
#   step01: data audit
#   step02: merged vs conditional coding: prevalence and one-dimensional latent class models
#   step03: robustness of one-dimensional models (employees, K = 1-8, local dependence, threshold)
#   step04: two-dimensional latent class model (need x compensation) and first Monte Carlo
#   step05: model scan, bootstrap, validation of compensation regimes, subgroups
#   step06: gradient under two group definitions; tables
#   step07: occupation, larger models, item deletion, stricter threshold, Monte Carlo S5-S9
#   step09: measurement assumption, random starts, threshold c = 4, excluded cases, Monte Carlo S10-S12
#   step10: model selection criteria, model-free respondent-level measure, simulation S13
#   step11: selected 6 x 5 model: profiles, bootstrap, subgroups, sensitivity, S13
#   step12: agreement (ARI) between merged and conditional one-dimensional typologies
#   step13: partial measurement invariance
#   Figures are produced at the end of the script.
# Each step is skipped if its output files already exist.
# Route A / Route B: if one approach fails, the other is used.
# =====================================================================

